      "refersTo": "button-poster",
      "description": "Cream call to action that lives only on the orange poster field.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-field\"><a class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-poster\" href=\"#\">Continue: 08:30 Overnight build failed <svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"/><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"/></svg></a></div>",
      "css": ".ds-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;height:36px;padding:0 14px;border-radius:3px;font:500 14px/1 'Archivo Variable',Archivo,ui-sans-serif,sans-serif;border:0;cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 150ms,color 150ms;white-space:nowrap}.ds-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#2f4e9c);outline-offset:2px}.ds-btn:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}.ds-field{background:var(--poster,#d4691f);padding:24px}.ds-btn-poster{height:44px;padding:0 20px;font-size:15px;text-decoration:none;background:var(--rail-active,#f6eedf);color:var(--rail-active-ink,#1d1a17)}.ds-btn-poster:hover{background:var(--surface,#fffcf7)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input-field",
      "description": "Warm-white field, strong hairline, navy caret and focus ring.",
      "html": "<input class=\"ds-input\" placeholder=\"Paste a job ad\" />",
      "css": ".ds-input{width:280px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong,#bcb1a2);border-radius:3px;background:var(--surface,#fffcf7);color:var(--ink,#1e1b18);padding:8px 12px;font:400 14px 'Archivo Variable',Archivo,sans-serif;caret-color:var(--primary,#2f4e9c)}.ds-input::placeholder{color:var(--ink-3,#6b6258)}.ds-input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#2f4e9c);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rail Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-item",
      "description": "Orange rail, ink labels, cream active tile.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-rail\"><a class=\"ds-nav ds-nav-active\" href=\"#\">Today</a><a class=\"ds-nav\" href=\"#\">Theory</a><a class=\"ds-nav\" href=\"#\">SQL gym</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-rail{background:var(--rail,#d4691f);padding:12px 8px;width:216px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;height:36px;padding:0 10px;border-radius:3px;font:500 14px 'Archivo Variable',Archivo,sans-serif;color:var(--rail-ink,#1d1a17);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 150ms}.ds-nav:hover{background:var(--rail-hover,#df7d36)}.ds-nav-active,.ds-nav-active:hover{background:var(--rail-active,#f6eedf);color:var(--rail-active-ink,#1d1a17)}.ds-nav:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#2f4e9c);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Discipline Tag and Status Pills",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "status-pill",
      "description": "Flag square with pictogram plus name; soft status pills.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-row\"><span class=\"ds-tag\"><span class=\"ds-sq\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"10\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"9.5\" y=\"10\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"10\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"16\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"9.5\" y=\"16\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/><rect x=\"16\" y=\"16\" width=\"5\" height=\"4\"/></svg></span>SQL</span><span class=\"ds-pill ds-ok\">Correct</span><span class=\"ds-pill ds-bad\">Incorrect</span><span class=\"ds-pill ds-info\">For Claude</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-row{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;font-family:'Archivo Variable',Archivo,sans-serif}.ds-tag{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink-2,#4a433c)}.ds-sq{display:inline-flex;width:18px;height:18px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:2px;background:var(--d-sql,#2f4e9c);color:var(--on-d-sql,#fbf6ee)}.ds-pill{border-radius:2px;padding:2px 6px;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}.ds-ok{background:var(--ok-soft,#e8eed8);color:var(--ok,#4f6b1f)}.ds-bad{background:var(--bad-soft,#f8e3e1);color:var(--bad,#b3323c)}.ds-info{background:var(--primary-soft,#e4e9f5);color:var(--primary,#2f4e9c)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Flat warm-white sheet with hairline-ruled rows; no shadow.",
      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-panel\"><div class=\"ds-ph\"><h3>Licence status</h3><p>Practise or sit the exam to get a level</p></div><div class=\"ds-pb\">L3 · Full licence</div></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{width:320px;background:var(--surface,#fffcf7);border:1px solid var(--line,#ddd4c7);font-family:'Archivo Variable',Archivo,sans-serif}.ds-ph{padding:12px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#ddd4c7)}.ds-ph h3{margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:680;color:var(--ink,#1e1b18)}.ds-ph p{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-3,#6b6258)}.ds-pb{padding:12px 20px;font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2,#4a433c)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Programme Strip in Ticked Frame",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "programme-band",
      "description": "Signature: flag-banded event cells inside the poster tick border.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-poster\"><div class=\"ds-tf\"><ol class=\"ds-strip\"><li><span class=\"ds-band\" style=\"background:#5c6d26;color:#fbf6ee\">08:30</span><span class=\"ds-ev\">Overnight build failed</span></li><li><span class=\"ds-band\" style=\"background:#b84e17;color:#fbf6ee\">09:15</span><span class=\"ds-ev\">Stand-up and a vague request</span></li><li><span class=\"ds-band\" style=\"background:#2f4e9c;color:#fbf6ee\">10:00</span><span class=\"ds-ev\">Profile the sources</span></li></ol></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-poster{background:var(--poster,#d4691f);padding:24px}.ds-tf{position:relative;padding:16px;background:var(--tick-ground,#f1ebe1);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--tick,#1e1b18)}.ds-tf::before{content:'';position:absolute;inset:4px;pointer-events:none;background:repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tick,#1e1b18) 0 2.5px,transparent 2.5px 6px) top/100% 8px no-repeat,repeating-linear-gradient(90deg,var(--tick,#1e1b18) 0 2.5px,transparent 2.5px 6px) bottom/100% 8px no-repeat,repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,var(--tick,#1e1b18) 0 2.5px,transparent 2.5px 6px) left/8px 100% no-repeat,repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,var(--tick,#1e1b18) 0 2.5px,transparent 2.5px 6px) right/8px 100% no-repeat}.ds-strip{position:relative;outline:1.5px solid var(--tick,#1e1b18);display:flex;gap:3px;margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;font-family:'Archivo Variable',Archivo,sans-serif}.ds-strip li{flex:1;min-width:110px;background:var(--surface,#fffcf7);display:flex;flex-direction:column}.ds-band{height:28px;display:flex;align-items:center;padding:0 8px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-ev{padding:8px;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;font-stretch:78%;line-height:1.15;color:var(--ink,#1e1b18)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Poster Lettering",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "typography.display",
      "description": "Cream uppercase Federo lockup on the poster field.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-poster ds-lock\"><h1>The analytics engineer’s day</h1><p>Tidepool Coffee Co.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-poster{background:var(--poster,#d4691f);padding:32px}.ds-lock{text-align:center;color:var(--poster-ink,#f6eedf);font-family:Federo,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.01em;text-transform:uppercase}.ds-lock h1{margin:0 auto;max-width:16ch;font-weight:400;font-size:56px;line-height:.95}.ds-lock p{margin:16px 0 0;font-size:28px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The 1912 Official Programme",
    "overview": "The app is printed matter for one analytics engineer's Olympiad, after Olle Hjortzberg's Stockholm 1912 poster (pinned by the user). A saturated poster orange carries the shell; cream Jugendstil lettering announces titles; the flag colours of the competing nations become ten discipline colours, each paired with its own pictogram; and the poster's border, a cream band of black ticks between two ink rules, frames the moments that matter: the day's programme and the licence plate you leave with.\n\nBelow the poster, the work happens on a warm stone ground with warm-white sheets: hairline-ruled tables, flat panels, small 3px corners, no decorative shadow. It is a dense, keyboard-first operating surface. The theory pages are long-form reading inside the same world. Light is the daytime desk and dark is a warm night ground; both are first-class and every token has a dark counterpart.\n\nThe world refuses the grey SaaS learning dashboard (card grids, progress rings, purple gradients) and the dark-IDE neon costume.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Poster orange shell rail and poster field, ink labels, cream active tile.",
      "Cream Federo lettering, uppercase, for page titles, the home and exam hero, and level plates only.",
      "Ten flag colours, each bound to one discipline and one pictogram, used as full-strength bands and squares.",
      "The ticked frame as the single ornamental device, reused in exactly two places.",
      "Flat stone and warm-white surfaces separated by hairline rules.",
      "Archivo for everything you read or operate; JetBrains Mono for code and data."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Poster Orange Rule",
        "body": "Orange is the field, never a control. It belongs to the shell rail, the poster field, and the licence plate; buttons, links and data on stone never take it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flag Band Rule",
        "body": "A flag colour means one discipline and nothing else. It always appears with that discipline's pictogram or name, at full strength, with its paired on-colour for anything placed on it. Never use a flag colour for status, emphasis, or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cream On Orange Rule",
        "body": "Cream on poster orange is about 3.1:1. It is for lettering at 24px and above and for filled cream tiles carrying ink text. Small text on the orange field is rail ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lettering Only Rule",
        "body": "Federo is for page titles, the poster hero, and level plates, always uppercase and never below 24px. It never sets UI labels, buttons, table text, or body copy.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Times, counts, scores and percentages use tabular numerals so the programme and standings columns hold still.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Programme Rule",
        "body": "Panels, cells, tables and buttons are flat. Separation is a field change or a 1px rule. A shadow appears only on a true overlay.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep poster orange for the rail, the poster field and the licence plate, with rail ink for any small text on it.",
      "Do set page titles, the poster hero and level plates in uppercase Federo at 24px or more, and everything else in Archivo.",
      "Do show a discipline as its flag colour plus its pictogram or name, using the paired on-colour on top.",
      "Do separate programme cells and section segments with the 3px gap, and panel rows with 1px hairlines.",
      "Do use tabular numerals for times, counts and scores.",
      "Do define every new colour token for both light and dark."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't build the grey SaaS learning dashboard: card grids, progress rings, purple gradients.",
      "Don't dress code surfaces in a dark-IDE neon costume; the editor uses the poster syntax palette on code paper.",
      "Don't use a flag colour for status, emphasis or decoration, or mix two disciplines' colours in one mark.",
      "Don't put shadows on panels, cells, tables or buttons; only a true overlay is lifted.",
      "Don't add the ticked frame to new surfaces casually; it marks the day's programme and the licence result.",
      "Don't set small cream text on poster orange."
    ]
  }
}